              "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
              "markdown": "![What is the Smallest Size Available for Certified Diamonds?](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/09242103-2330-0066-0000-23a63aec4ec0:4)\nA diamond certificate is `an official grading report issued by an independent gemological laboratory that details a diamond's quality, measurements, and characteristics`.[[1]](https://www.shaneco.com/jewelry-education/diamond-certificates)[[2]](https://www.facebook.com/lapatiala/videos/ever-wonder-what-a-diamond-certification-actually-means-a-certified-diamond-has-/1448923110287248/)\n\n### What is Included\n\n- **The 4Cs** : Carat weight, cut, color, and clarity grades.\n- **Physical measurements** : Dimensions, polish, symmetry, and fluorescence.\n- **Origin details** : Whether the stone is natural or laboratory-grown.\n- **Laser inscription** : A unique report number inscribed directly on the diamond's girdle.[[1]](https://www.gia.edu/gem-lab-service/diamond-grading)[[2]](https://www.igi.org/)[[3]](https://www.facebook.com/lapatiala/videos/ever-wonder-what-a-diamond-certification-actually-means-a-certified-diamond-has-/1448923110287248/)[[4]](https://www.shaneco.com/jewelry-education/diamond-certificates)[[5]](https://www.google.com/search?q=product&prds=pvt:hg,productid:4248095270369679530,catalogid:5788861530722650871,gpcid:7124748820833785628&ibp=oshop)\n\n### Top Grading Laboratories\n\n- **[GIA](https://www.gia.edu/gem-lab-service/diamond-grading) (Gemological Institute of America)** : The most trusted and widely recognized authority for natural diamond grading.[[1]](https://stienhardt.com/blogs/education/diamond-certification-guide/)\n- **[IGI](https://www.igi.org/) (International Gemological Institute)** : Globally prominent and frequently utilized for both natural and lab-grown diamonds.[[1]](https://www.igi.org/)[[2]](https://stienhardt.com/blogs/education/diamond-certification-guide/)\n- **AGS (American Gem Society)** : Highly regarded for precision cut-grading and light performance analysis.[[1]](https://stienhardt.com/blogs/education/diamond-certification-guide/)\n\nIf you are looking to buy or evaluate a stone, tell me:\n\n- Are you shopping for a **natural or lab-grown** diamond?\n- What **carat size** or **budget** do you have in mind?\n\nI can help you understand which certification matters most for your purchase.",
